  "description": "LUYZEM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H80 Cl4 N28 O16 Tb8. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 3 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 3 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 3 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.735-3.869 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.66-111.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H80Cl4N28O16Tb8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Tb(III).",
